    "input": "search_document: Hello. I understand you are in a hurry and need a quick, simple answer.\n\n**Yes, the $25 diagnostic fee is true.**\nIf your bike is **outside** the warranty period, or if the problem is caused by misuse, there is a flat **$25 fee** to check the bike. [warranty]\n\n**Yes, you get the $25 back if you fix it.**\nIf you approve the repair, the **$25 fee is credited** (subtracted) from the final bill. You do not pay extra for the check if you proceed with the repair. [warranty]\n\n**Important Note:**\nIf your bike is **inside** the 2-year warranty period and the problem is a defect (not misuse), the repair is **free**. There is no $25 fee in that case. [warranty]\n\n**Regarding your request to call:**\nI am an online support assistant. **I cannot make phone calls.** I can only reply here in writing. [handbook_excerpts_do_not_cover_phone_support]\n\n**What you should do now:**\n1.  Tell the shop staff your bike is not working.\n2.  Ask them to check if it is under warranty.\n3.  If it is **out of warranty**, ask for the repair quote. Remember, the $25 check fee will be taken off the total price if you say \"yes\" to the repair.\n4.  If you say \"no\" to the repair, you will keep the $25 fee. [warranty]\n\nI hope this helps you get your bike fixed for your camping trip.",
